  "goodToKnow": "Das Zivilrecht is civil law, governing relations between private individuals and companies: contracts, property, family and inheritance. Its core is the Bürgerliches Gesetzbuch (BGB), in force since 1 January 1900 and admired and copied abroad. Synonyms: das Privatrecht, das bürgerliche Recht. It contrasts with das Strafrecht (criminal law) and das öffentliche Recht (public law). Zivilrechtlich means under civil law."
